 has not been chosen yet, on purpose.[48;2;61;1;0m[68X[38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m[5;8H5 +  [38;2;248;248;242mworks on any static[1Chost or un[2Cr any sub-path.   [1C      [1C[9X[10C  [1C  [1C   [1C    [1C  [1C   [1C      [38;2;80;200;80m[6;8H6 +[38;2;248;248;242m- It is hosted[1Con[1CGitHub[1CPages,[1Cat[1C`https://hdaraujo.github.io/metro/`.[1CThe[m[7;3H [1C [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 17 +  [38;2;248;248;242m`.github/workflows/pages.yml` workflow runs on every push to `main` and on demand: `npm ci`,[69X[38;2;80;200;80m[8;6H 18 +  [38;2;248;248;242m`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, then it uploads `dist/` and deploys it. The[73X[38;2;80;200;80m[9;6H 19 +  [38;2;248;248;242mrepository's Pages source must be set to "GitHub Actions". The Playwright tests are not part[69X[38;2;80;200;80m[10;6H 20 +  [38;2;248;248;242mof the workflow.[145X[49m[2m[11;6H 21 [22m - The build is a single bundle. MapLibre alone is about 1 MB, and the chunk-size warning limit is[K[2m[12;6H 22 [22m   raised to allow it.[K[2m[13;6H 23 [22m - MapLibre GL 6 loads its web worker from a file next to its own module, and a bundle has no such[K[m[14;3H⎿[1C Updated [1mplays\003-setup-github-page\intent.md[22m (+1 -0)[K[38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m[15;7H1 +[38;2;248;248;242mhelp me setup a github page fo[2Cthis[1Crepo    [m[16;3H⎿[1C Allowed[1Cby[1Cauto[1Cmode[1Cclassifier[17;6H[K[38;2;153;153;153m[18;3HRan [1m1[22m shell command[K[m[19;3H[K[38;2;255;255;255m
●[m[1CI've set up GitHub Pages deployment[1Cand[1Ccommitted[1Cit[1Con[1Cthe[1Cplay's[1Cbranch,[38;2;177;185;249m[1C003-setup-github-page[m[1C(commit[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cb19660e[m).[1CIt[1Chasn't[1Cbeen[1Cpushed.[1CLint,[1Cthe[1C90[1Cunit[1Ctests[1Cand[1Cthe[21;3Hproduction[1Cbuild[1Call[1Cpass[1Clocally.[1CThe[1Cworkflow[1Citself[1Chasn't[1Crun[1Con[1CGitHub[1Cyet.[22;6H[K[1m[23;3HWhat I added[22m[K[24;3H-[38;2;177;185;249m[1m[1C.github/workflows/pages.yml[m[1m:[22m on every push to [38;2;177;185;249mmain[m, or when you start it by hand from the Actions tab, it installs dependencies, lints, runs the unit tests, builds, and deploys[38;2;177;185;249m[25;5Hdist/ [mto Pages. It doesn't run the Playwright end-to-end tests.[K[26;3H-[1m[1CNo app changes:[22m the build already uses relative paths, so the app, manifest and service worker work unchanged at [38;2;177;185;249mhttps://hdaraujo.github.io/metro/[m.[K[27;3H-[1m[1CDocs:[22m I updated the Deployment section of [38;2;177;185;249mREADME.md[m, the hosting notes in [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/modules/app-platform.md[m, and the deployment line in [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/tech.md[m,[1Cwhich[28;5Hused to say the host was undecided. I also filled in the play's [38;2;177;185;249mintent.md[m. The play's other files ([38;2;177;185;249mCLAUDE.md[m, [38;2;177;185;249mconfig.yaml[m, [38;2;177;185;249mpositions.yaml[m, [38;2;177;185;249msessions/[m) are left uncommitted[1Cfor[29;5HBuilding to manage.[K[30;6H[K[1m[31;3HWhat you need to do on GitHub[22m[1C([38;2;177;185;249mgh[m[1Cisn't[1Cinstalled[1Chere,[1Cso[1CI[1Ccouldn't):[32;3H1.[1CIn the repo, go to [1mSettings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source[22m and choose [1mGitHub Actions[22m. This is[1Ca[1Cone-time[1Csetting.[33;3H2. Push and merge: [38;2;177;185;249mgit push -u origin 003-setup-github-page[m,[1Cthen[1Cmerge[1Cinto[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cmain[m.[1CThe[1Cfirst[1Cdeploy[1Cruns[1Con[1Cthat[1Cpush.[1CBy[1Cdefault,[1CGitHub[1Conly[1Clets[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cmain[m[1Cdeploy[1Cto[1CPages,[1Cso[34;6Hstarting the workflow from this branch won't publish anything.[K[35;3H[K[1m
